==English==
{{wikipedia|anticlimax}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|anti-|climax}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|aɪmæks}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|anticlimaxes}}

# A [[failed]] or [[reverse]] [[climax]], ''[[particularly]]'':
## {{lb|en|narratology}} An [[unsatisfying]] [[resolution]] to a [[narrative]], [[usually]] [[owing to]] a ''[[deus ex machina]]'' or [[similarly]] [[trivial]] [[resolution]] of the [[main]] [[conflict]].
## {{lb|en|rhetoric}} An [[abrupt]] [[descent]] ([[either]] [[deliberate]] or [[unintentional]]) from the [[dignity]] of the [[idea]] which the [[speaker]] or [[writer]] [[appear]]ed to be [[aiming]] for.

